Rules:
  [C1] Use `auto` for type inference.
  [C2] Use range-based for loops.
  [C3] Use `std::unique_ptr` for exclusive ownership.
  [C4] Use `std::shared_ptr` for shared ownership.
  [C5] Use `std::vector` by default.
  [C6] Use `const` correctness.
  [C7] Use `nullptr` instead of `NULL`.
  [C8] Use `std::string` instead of C strings.

Pros:
  - Maximum performance
  - Hardware control
  - Large ecosystem

Cons:
  - Manual memory management
  - Undefined behavior
  - Long compile times

Alternatives:
  - Rust (safer)
  - Go (simpler)
  - Zig (modern)

State: +

